# Build context for server/Dockerfile is the repo root. The final image only
# needs server/**, src/** and Version, but the web-client build stage (see
# the Dockerfile) also needs client-web/**, client-desktop/**, build-scripts/
# (npm run build:licenses), and the root package.json/package-lock.json —
# everything below this comment is either desktop-only (src-electron,
# Installer, Dotnet) or build tooling neither stage needs, that would
# otherwise be uploaded to the daemon on every build.
.git
.github
node_modules
build
coverage

Dotnet
src-electron
Installer
images
README
*.md

.vscode
.idea
*.log

# NOTE: `src/**` is deliberately kept whole. It is tempting to drop
# src/components and src/views since the server renders nothing, but
# src/stores/gameLog/index.js imports a pure helper from
# src/views/GameLog/sessions/buildGameLogSessions.js, and future upstream
# merges can add more edges like it. Text source is cheap; a container that
# fails to resolve an import at runtime is not.
